  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (resnet50) is weak at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether leveraging multiple cellular profiles with aggregation can improve the RNA baseline beyond the single-profile PCA result. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile + avgpool with the same pca_n2000 encoder, providing a clean, near-single-variable comparison to config_001 (only the profile/aggregation structure changes). It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it isolates the effect of profile multiplicity and aggregation without confounding encoder choice, (2) avgpool is a low-risk, simple aggregator that is less likely to fail than a transformer with limited data, and (3) the result directly informs whether the multiprofile axis is worth further exploration (e.g., with scvi/scgpt encoders) or whether we should instead invest in encoder quality or multimodal fusion next."
}

